<br>
</FONT><P><P><i></i></TD></TR><TR BGCOLOR=#e6ebd7><TD NOWRAP width=20% valign=top align=left><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2><A HREF=http://pub2.ezboard.com/upoisin.showPublicProfile>Poisin</A>&nbsp; <IMG SRC=http://www.ezboard.com/intl/aenglish/image/globalBlack.gif BORDER=0 WIDTH=10 HEIGHT=10></FONT></B><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>Global user</FONT><BR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>(</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>2/24/00</FONT> <FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1 COLOR=#333399>9:50:08 am</FONT><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=1>)<BR></FONT></TD><TD VALIGN=TOP ALIGN=LEFT><B><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Re: Druid only quest items..</FONT></B><HR><FONT FACE="Verdana,Arial" SIZE=2>Saddens me greatly about how you druids have no questable items.<br>
<br>
I just want to point out that you are a little misled on the cleric quests.  In every case, there is a easy/common drop item. Much like a few other class quests.<br>
<br>
However, the second piece to our quest armour is located on rare spawns.  Don't forget the fact that most of us don't have access to teleport, tracking, kiting or sow.  Now given the fact that we need to travel to-<br>
<br>
Permafrost- rare glacier bear (8 hr spawn with ph)<br>
Befallen- rare babinsbort (7 hr spawn with ph)<br>
Kerra Ridge- rare maugrim (20 min spawn with ph)<br>
Rathe Mountains- rare dark giant skel (20 min spawn with ph)<br>
Kithikor- rare ingot drop (8 hr spawn)<br>
N Karanas- rare ghoul which is KOS by close NPCs (unknown timing)<br>
Dagnors' Cauldron- Bilge (need I say more?)<br>
OOT- rare gull skytalon (8 hr spawn with ph)<br>
<br>
The easy peices of the quest are easy- but they are usually picked up by everyone because of that nice little bag on the floor- Hey! it might be a Mammo cloak, lets pick it up-<br>
<br>
Now since the patch, the chestguard has been moved off bilge to another NPC, shamen and druids are hunting it while waiting for bilge to craft a cleric quest peice they think they can trade for that KPT or reed belt.  Gull has been beefed up so that a cleric needs to be 44 to solo it (we have limited solo ability), not to mention the shamen killing gull while waiting for thier NPC to show.<br>
<br>
Just an FYI on the time it takes to camp and get some of the items...<br>
<br>
Shield- 22 hours, killed once<br>
Mace- 16 hours, killed once<br>
boots- 6 hours<br>
arms- 21 hours<br>
legs- 7 hours<br>
gloves- 16 hours, uncompleted<br>
bracers- not even going to try<br>
chestguard- not even going to try<br>
<br>
I was lvl 42-43 when attempting these quests.  I would hate to see the intended level for these quests (30-40) gather thier 3-4 buddies and kill a rare in a day. Would you do it?  I have had ppl say sure! But they leave after 2 hours or so.<br>
<br>
After all is said and done, the armour looks great has nice resistances and a couple irrelevant stat modifiers, is the only armour WORSE than the old rubi, weighs a tonne and eats up our money resources worse than the symbol spell componenets, our spells, purchase of teleports/sow/..., not to mention kills 60+ hours to get a couple peices.<br>
<br>
